# LF everywhere, on every machine. The site is built and run on Linux, and the deploy package is
# zipped from the working tree: with core.autocrlf=true on Windows, the shell scripts, systemd
# units and sudoers file were checked out with CRLF and broke on the server (sudoers failed
# visudo; bash chokes on $'\r'). This overrides autocrlf for this repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.otf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.zip binary
